  "notes": "UKing sells the same 8ch RGBW par chart across ZQ01069 (18x8W, 110 W, 2.07 kg net, 22x22x30 cm box, 25 deg), ZQ01061/B117 (18x8W, 108 W, 2.95 kg, 25x16x26 cm) and ZQ01424 (14 LEDs); the 8ch chart (Dimmer,R,G,B,W,Strobe,Function,Speed) is identical in the ZQ01069 manual, the ZQ01424 manual and OFL's B117 definition. Physical values here are ZQ01069's. CONFLICT with repo: the repo's 'Uking Par' 7ch map (OFL par-light-b262: Dimmer,R,G,B,Strobe,Mode,Hue) is the 36x1W RGB par with NO white channel; the 8ch RGBW chart inserts White at CH5 and shifts Strobe to CH6, Macro to CH7, Speed to CH8. Which physical par the venue owns decides which chart applies; if the fixture is patched at 8ch it is the RGBW unit. Amazon listings (B0BFQWBGCX '216W', B07PZF87HZ '18x12W') do not print the chart; the marketing wattage exceeds the manual's rated 110 W."
